                <pb facs="0680" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg562"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/6287: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-29T15:00:00-05:45">April 29, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>122. Orders issued for discontinuance of all marine posts on the Coco River from
                    the Poteca River eastward. Several other posts in the eastern area also being
                    abandoned. Fifteen officers and two hundred and fifty men being withdrawn
                    tomorrow on the transport <hi rendition="#italic">Bridge</hi>. It is anticipated
                    that by July 1st marine forces will be reduced to twenty-five hundred regular
                    forces and three hundred aviation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
